{id:"jv12",title:"Project: Monkey toolkit",sub:"build a set of helper methods",project:true,steps:[
 {type:"talk",title:"Build your own toolbox",mood:"cheer",
  body:`<p>Programmers collect small, well-named helper methods. You'll write three: one that checks prime numbers, one that reverses words, and one that rates a password.</p>`,
  say:"Good method names make code read like a sentence."},
 {type:"code",title:"Step 1: isPrime",body:`<p>Write ${C("static boolean isPrime(int n)")}. A prime is bigger than 1 and only divides evenly by 1 and itself. Then the loop prints every prime up to 20.</p>`,start:`// write isPrime here\n\nfor (int i = 1; i <= 20; i++) {\n  if (isPrime(i)) System.out.print(i + " ");\n}\nSystem.out.println();\n`,
  use:[[/static\s+boolean\s+isPrime\s*\(\s*int/,"Start with static boolean isPrime(int n)."]],out:["2 3 5 7 11 13 17 19"],variants:[[/i <= 20/,"i <= 10",["2 3 5 7"]]],
  hint:`static boolean isPrime(int n) {\n  if (n < 2) return false;\n  for (int d = 2; d * d <= n; d++) {\n    if (n % d == 0) return false;\n  }\n  return true;\n}\n\nfor (int i = 1; i <= 20; i++) {\n  if (isPrime(i)) System.out.print(i + " ");\n}\nSystem.out.println();`},
 {type:"code",title:"Step 2: reverse",body:`<p>Write ${C("static String reverse(String s)")} that gives back the word backwards. Then check if a word is a palindrome (the same both ways).</p>`,start:`// write reverse here\n\nString w = "racecar";\nSystem.out.println(reverse(w));\nSystem.out.println(reverse(w).equals(w));\n`,
  use:[[/static\s+String\s+reverse\s*\(\s*String/,"Start with static String reverse(String s)."],[/charAt/,"Build it one character at a time with charAt."]],out:["racecar","true"],variants:[[/"racecar"/,"\"monkey\"",["yeknom","false"]]],
  hint:`static String reverse(String s) {\n  String out = "";\n  for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    out += s.charAt(i);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nString w = "racecar";\nSystem.out.println(reverse(w));\nSystem.out.println(reverse(w).equals(w));`},
 {type:"code",title:"Step 3: password rater",body:`<p>Write ${C("static String rate(String pw)")}: return ${C("weak")} if it's shorter than 8 characters, ${C("strong")} if it's 8+ <b>and</b> has a digit, otherwise ${C("okay")}. ${C("Character.isDigit(c)")} checks one character.</p>`,start:`// write rate here\n\nSystem.out.println(rate("ook"));\nSystem.out.println(rate("bananarama"));\nSystem.out.println(rate("banana42ok"));\n`,
  use:[[/Character\.isDigit/,"Use Character.isDigit(...) to spot numbers."]],out:["weak","okay","strong"],
  hint:`static String rate(String pw) {\n  if (pw.length() < 8) return "weak";\n  for (int i = 0; i < pw.length(); i++) {\n    if (Character.isDigit(pw.charAt(i))) return "strong";\n  }\n  return "okay";\n}\n\nSystem.out.println(rate("ook"));\nSystem.out.println(rate("bananarama"));\nSystem.out.println(rate("banana42ok"));`},
 {type:"done"}]}
